                "title": "Keep paddle shaft seals greased",
                "value": "",
                "pdf_link": "<p>Grease seals daily to prevent material from leaking around the paddle shaft and getting into the bearings.</p><p>If mixer is running all day, grease at mid-day and at the end of the day. Grease at the end of use will help push material that may have gotten into the seal out before it sets up.</p><p>Material build up within the seal will wear grooves in the shaft causing the seals to fail, and damage shaft resulting in costly repairs.</p>"
