              "type": "capability-card",
              "settings": {
                "icon": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 9\" fill=\"none\">\n  <path d=\"M0.5 4.5H10.5M6.50003 8.5L10.5 4.5L6.50003 0.5\" stroke=\"#2D2926\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>",
                "title": "Change paddle shaft seals at first sign of leakage.",
                "value": "",
                "pdf_link": "<p>If material is leaking through the seal be sure to changes seals before the material reaches the bearings causing the bearings to fail.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "capability_card_fPAQ8E"
          ]
        },
        "capability_column_HFCzPd": {
          "type": "capability-column",
          "settings": {},
          "blocks": {
            "capability_card_9UQpqX": {
              "type": "capability-card",
              "settings": {
                "icon": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 9\" fill=\"none\">\n  <path d=\"M0.5 4.5H10.5M6.50003 8.5L10.5 4.5L6.50003 0.5\" stroke=\"#2D2926\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>",
                "title": "Service engine",
                "value": "",
                "pdf_link": "<p>Keeping the engine serviced prevents excessive wear on the engine. Change engine oil regularly according to engine recommendations. Keep air filter clean and change as needed. Keep excessive material build up off of engine. Material build up around or on the engine can restrict air flow that keeps the engine cool.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "capability_card_9UQpqX"
          ]
        },
        "capability_column_PCqBJX": {
          "type": "capability-column",
          "settings": {},
          "blocks": {
            "capability_card_aq3qG8": {
              "type": "capability-card",
              "settings": {
                "icon": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 9\" fill=\"none\">\n  <path d=\"M0.5 4.5H10.5M6.50003 8.5L10.5 4.5L6.50003 0.5\" stroke=\"#2D2926\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>",
                "title": "Do not over adjust paddle rubbers.",
                "value": "",
                "pdf_link": "<p>Paddle rubbers should be adjust to where they are slightly away from the inside of the drum. If the rubbers fold back on the paddle they are adjusted too tight. This will cause stretching and cracking of the paddle rubber. Over adjusted paddle rubbers also cause wear on the thickness of the drum resulting in holes worn in drum.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "capability_card_aq3qG8"
          ]
